/*
  ComputedMetricEditor.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0182 · ComputedMetricEditor (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  ComputedMetricEditor resolves (table "ComputedMetricEditor") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  Group 1 mirrors the exact key set extracted from the web source
  (features/notifications/components/ComputedMetricEditor.tsx) — the field labels, the
  empty-choice prompts, the threshold prompt, and the live-preview line/verdict. Group
  1b backs the operator labels (web `t('metricOps.<opKey>', opLabel)`); the dynamic
  metric-name and window keys (`metricNames.<id>` / `metricWindows.<window>`) are
  backend-driven, so — exactly as the web does — they resolve through their runtime
  fallback rather than a static catalog entry. Group 2 backs the native-only chrome
  (freshness / empty / error / offline / retry) the Apple HIG states contract requires
  for the `useAlertMetrics` source + the preview mutation.
*/

